      "key": "mideast",
      "name": "Middle East war & Gulf shipping",
      "sa_impact": "Fuel: Australia imports most of its fuel, much of it refined from Gulf crude in Asia. Shipping attacks or a Hormuz closure push up prices within days and can cause local shortages.",
      "why": "Before the 2024-25 Israel-Iran exchanges and US strikes, watchers saw US tanker surges toward Europe and the Gulf, embassy departure orders, regional GPS jamming, airspace closures and oil price jumps, often 1-3 days ahead.",
